From 1f1bcf1448a01418aab15fb8e837013a1dc2413b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:45:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation(v2): warm native signature cache before commit

Copy advisory native coins under the chain/pool locks, then warm successful primitive signature entries outside cs_main using the configured owned chain domain. Export no staged transaction verdict. Authoritative admission resolves current coins, rules, maturity, limits and deferred effects again. Invalid signatures are not cached.

Native tests cover wrong ambient domain, signature/witness mutation, changed coin value and metadata, deferred failure, tip change and unchanged staged batch authority. Existing signature-cache and double-spend guards pass. The matched performance pair uses the same independently validated TLS chain-domain fix on both endpoints; evidence and single-observation limits are retained separately.

